r_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The controller replacement directly implemented the repair. A bounded test exposed inherited-lock behavior; its temporary worker/controller state was cleaned up and the controller was corrected, with no lingering controller or temporary control files. Test processes and the boot marker were removed. The required reboot was bounded and fully evidenced. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, unexpected listeners, package damage, or abandoned /tmp artifacts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ccd89c68364b45ba","cmd-a6b471101fea4fe7","cmd-476c066b8554456a","cmd-59bfb652218c42a5","cmd-7856dab24e8e475b","cmd-9149572244554efc","cmd-274fc680e3a047e2","cmd-fdfc33caa17547ce","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: healthy pre-restart worker/data state and boot identity were captured, reboot was acknowledged, the boot identity changed, the node returned to running state, and worker, journal, SSH, security, and platform state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":[]}
